  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 8 actions (actions.js, one object literal returned by getActionDefinitions) and 3 boolean feedbacks (feedbacks.js). Presets (presets.js) are not catalogued.",
    "The device is fixed to 4 inputs and 2 outputs: self.INPUT (\"In 1\"..\"In 4\") and self.OUTPUT (\"Out 1\", \"Out 2\") are hard-coded in index.js (lines 23-33). All dropdowns are therefore closed lists with string ids. The \"MMX 42/62\" in the manifest is not reflected by any model option.",
    "Protocol: TCPHelper to the configured host and port (config.js: default port 32100, regex Regex.PORT; the config also has a \"Save TCP Response\" checkbox). Commands are Extron SIS strings: \"<in>*<out>!\" (audio and video), \"%\" (video only), \"$\" (audio only), \"<out>*<0|1>B\" video mute, \"<out>*<0|1>Z\" audio mute, \"<0|1>*B\" / \"<0|1>*Z\" for all outputs, \"<in>*<level>\" gain, \"<in>+G\" / \"<in>-G\", \"<0|1>X\" front panel lock.",
    "The callbacks run the command string through parseVariablesInString and unescape, but all inputs are dropdowns, so no variables can be entered.",
    "The VideoMute/AudioMute actions use the choice id \"All\" for all outputs, while the mute_status feedback uses the id \"0\" for the same meaning.",
    "AudioLevel choices are generated by a loop (43 entries from +24 dB down to -18 dB, id = abs(value) + \"G\" for >= 0 and + \"g\" for < 0, label with explicit \"+\"/\"-\" sign, so 0 is \"+0dB\" with id \"0G\"); the catalog lists them as written.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.11.2: options do not support expressions."
  ]
}
